1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
First, we choose a circle tool, click and drag your mouse in the 2D window to form a circle, press the Ctrl key to form a positive circle.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The widest part of this circle is twice as wide as your head.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:25,000
After selecting this board, click the positioning key in the upper right corner, then click on the virtual model, you can arrange this board near the head of the virtual model.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
This positioning symbol is like a handle, now the positioning ball is a double corner, you can see.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:41,000
If we directly press the Ctrl key to simulate, this board will fall on the head of the virtual model, because we have gravity in the 3D environment.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:51,000
We can return the gravity to 0 first, so that the gravity in the 3D space no longer works, and then let this hat stay above the head of the virtual model.

7
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
On the right side of the gravity, we adjust the value of gravity to 0,

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
and then look at the simulation, the 3D board will no longer have the influence of gravity.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
In order to prevent the board from moving, we can temporarily fix it on the virtual model.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Here we can use a function under the fake needle, called the function of fixing to the virtual model.

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Click on the board, then click on the head of the virtual model, this board will be fixed on the virtual model head, it will not move horizontally.

12
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Next, we are going to make this hat hat.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:34,000
For this hat, we can first select its outside panel line, and then click on the internal line border to draw an internal circle.

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:43,000
When we select this internal circle, the double center point will be retracted, and it will be retracted based on the center.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
So we can adjust this internal circle, which is the size of the hole we are going to dig later.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The basis of the size of this hole is that when we switch to the virtual model front,

17
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
we want to see that this hole is slightly larger than its head.

18
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
After we finish, we can select this internal circle in the middle, and then right-click to cut and sew.

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Then it will become the top of our hat later.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Next, we can arrange the position of this top of the hat in the 3D space,

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
